This project keeps its generated Graphify knowledge graph at `graphify-out/`.
If `graphify-out/graph.json` is missing, run `graphify extract . --code-only --out .` followed by `graphify cluster-only . --no-label` from the project root. The local graph covers code; documenting other files requires semantic extraction.

**MANDATORY: Before using Read, Grep, Glob, or Bash to explore the codebase, you MUST run graphify first:**
- `graphify query "<question>"` — scoped subgraph for any codebase or architecture question
- `graphify path "<A>" "<B>"` — dependency path between two symbols
- `graphify explain "<concept>"` — all nodes related to a concept

This applies to YOU and to every subagent you spawn. Include this rule explicitly in every subagent prompt that involves code exploration. Do not skip graphify because files are "already known" or because you are executing a plan — the graph surfaces cross-file relationships that grep and Read can miss.

Only use Read/Grep/Glob directly when:
1. graphify has already oriented you and you need to modify or debug specific lines
2. `graphify-out/graph.json` does not exist yet

- If `graphify-out/wiki/index.md` exists, navigate it instead of reading raw files
- Read `graphify-out/GRAPH_REPORT.md` only for broad architecture review when query/path/explain do not surface enough context
- After modifying code files, run `graphify extract . --code-only --out .` to refresh the code graph, then `graphify cluster-only . --no-label` to refresh the report and HTML.
